cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Agentic Graph-RAG: Query-Conditional Retrieval Planning with a PIVOT
  Reasoning Loop
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the software and the
  accompanying paper.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Janis
    family-names: Poggemann
    affiliation: FH Münster University of Applied Sciences
repository-code: https://github.com/JanisPog/agentic-graph-rag
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23727940
abstract: >-
  A stateful agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation system over a Neo4j
  knowledge graph. A planner activates per-query retrieval arms (dense,
  BM25, graph-PPR, optional web search), RRF fusion and a cross-encoder
  reranker narrow the candidate set, CRAG grading gates context quality,
  and a PIVOT loop (Plan, Inspect, eVOlve, Verify) admits a retry only
  when an untried method is expected to score strictly higher. Queries
  that cannot be answered are deferred with a structured payload.
  Evaluated on the WixQA enterprise-support benchmark.
keywords:
  - retrieval-augmented generation
  - graph-rag
  - knowledge graph
  - information retrieval
  - agentic systems
  - neo4j
  - large language models
